@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@
+# UI sounds that played late
+
+## Cause
+
+`UiSounds.play` created a new `Sound` for every cue and destroyed it when it ended. Nothing kept
+the asset loaded between cues, so each new Sound waited on its asset before it could play
+(`IsLoaded` was false at `Play()`). That wait was the 0.3 to 0.5 s delay, longest on phones.
+`ContentProvider:PreloadAsync` at startup did not help: it fetches the asset once, but no Sound
+holds it afterward, so it is not kept loaded for later cues.
+
+## What changed
+
+- `UiSounds.luau` keeps a counted cache: one `Sound` per id under
+  `SoundService.UiSoundCache`, kept while anything holds it.
+  - `UiSounds.holdSound(id)` returns a release function. The last release destroys the cached
+    Sound one frame later, so a cue played right after the release still finds it.
+  - `UiSounds.play(id)` clones the cached Sound, which is already loaded, so the cue starts at
+    once. With no hold it falls back to the old behavior (a new Sound, which may be late).
+  - `UiSounds.isCached(id)` reports whether an id is cached right now.
+  - Holds do nothing outside a running game, so a UI Labs story caches nothing.
+- `Main.client.luau` (the HUD, always up) holds `Click` and `PickerOpen` for its whole life.
+  `Click` is the shared button sound every screen will use. `PickerOpen` plays the moment the
+  picker is built, from the Build button or the B key, so it has to be loaded before then.
+- `BlockPicker.luau` holds `PickerClose` while the picker is open and releases it when the
+  picker closes. When the picker is closed, only the two short HUD sounds stay loaded.
+- The `PreloadAsync` call is gone.
+
+New screens follow the same pattern: in the screen's component body, call
+`cleanup(UiSounds.holdSound(id))` for each sound that screen plays, leaving out `Click`, which
+the HUD already holds. The hold lasts as long as the screen's scope (for example, while its
+`show` is true).
+
+Known limit: if the picker is opened and closed again faster than `PickerClose` loads (under
+about half a second on a slow connection), that first close sound can still be late.
+
+## Checking it in Studio
+
+1. Start a playtest. To get phone-like loading, use the Device emulator, and set
+   File > Studio Settings > Network > Incoming Replication Lag if you want a slow connection.
+2. In Explorer, open `SoundService > UiSoundCache`. With build mode off it holds two Sounds,
+   named after the `Click` and `PickerOpen` ids.
+3. Press Build. A third Sound (`PickerClose`) appears. Close the picker: one frame later it is
+   gone again.
+4. To see what a cue played with, paste this into the command bar (client side), then click the
+   Build button and a tile. Each line should read `true`:
+
+   ```lua
+   game:GetService("SoundService").ChildAdded:Connect(function(child)
+   	if child:IsA("Sound") then
+   		task.defer(function()
+   			print(child.SoundId, "IsLoaded at play:", child.IsLoaded)
+   		end)
+   	end
+   end)
+   ```
+
+   Before this change the same check printed `false`.
+5. By ear: the click should land with the press, and the picker's open sound with the picker
+   appearing, on both PC and a phone (or the emulator).
